# Rust workspace test counts — EXACT values, not floors.
#
# Read by scripts/ci-test-count-gate.sh, which requires BOTH numbers from
# `scripts/test-count.sh --workspace` to EQUAL what is recorded here.
#
#     EXECUTED=<n>
#     SKIPPED=<n>
#
# WHY EQUALITY, AND WHY BOTH (D0-R7-01)
# This was a FLOOR whose protocol said "count goes UP freely", recorded as 1891 — a number
# predating the entire `runtime` crate, so the actual sat scores of tests above it. A test that
# started SKIPPING kept the floor satisfied forever: exactly the disappearance the guard exists
# to catch. D0-R6 had already fixed the MEASUREMENT (executed, not reported — a skip scores as
# a pass) and the blindness merely moved into the THRESHOLD. Third form of one bug in one file.
# SKIPPED is recorded too because a lone total is satisfiable two ways: one test deleted while
# another stops skipping leaves EXECUTED unchanged.
#
# PROTOCOL
#   * Any change to either number — up OR down — updates this file IN THE SAME COMMIT, with the
#     reason in the message. An unexplained increase is as much a signal as a decrease.
#   * A drop in EXECUTED needs the specific test named: removed on purpose, or started skipping?
#     The second is a defect wearing the first's clothes.
#
# NOT YET RECORDED — DELIBERATE. 1891 is known wrong, and `cargo test --workspace` cannot run on
# the dev box (`compositor` needs graphics headers that are absent there), so a workspace count
# is not obtainable outside CI. With no keys below, the gate FAILS and prints the measured pair
# to paste in. Failing loudly with the real number beats carrying one known to be wrong.
